MID_SE_Lor_Tob_C: <EDH>
MID_SE_Lor_Tob_C_001: How come I'm not catching anything here? Did they\nlie when they told me this was a prime fishing spot?
MID_SE_Lor_Tob_C_002: Oops, am I late to the party? *gulp* Ahhh.
MID_SE_Lor_Tob_C_003: Ugh, here comes the "mighty" commander. And he's\nbeen drinking too. Just great.
MID_SE_Lor_Tob_C_004: There's supposed to be tons of fish here. How about\nit? They biting for you?
MID_SE_Lor_Tob_C_005: Nah, not really. And I'm outta bait, so I was thinking\nI'd head back.
MID_SE_Lor_Tob_C_006: All out, huh? Then use mine. Here you go!
MID_SE_Lor_Tob_C_007: Huh? Look, big guy, I didn't ask.
MID_SE_Lor_Tob_C_008: No worries, kiddo. My mashed-up bait is special.\nGive it a try.
MID_SE_Lor_Tob_C_009: Special, huh? Alright, let's see how special it is.
MID_SE_Lor_Tob_C_010: Whoa, I've already got a bite! And it's a big one!
MID_SE_Lor_Tob_C_011: Here, let me help. On three, pull!
MID_SE_Lor_Tob_C_012: Thanks, man! One, two, three, now!
MID_SE_Lor_Tob_C_013: Baw haw haw! Look at the size of it! A big fish\nlike that oughta make a great snack.
MID_SE_Lor_Tob_C_014: That's...that's amazing! Not bad for an old guy.
MID_SE_Lor_Tob_C_015: Hey, I'm from Saramis. This kinda thing is second\nnature for us seafaring types.
MID_SE_Lor_Tob_C_016: On a ship, knowing how to fish is the difference\nbetween life and death.
MID_SE_Lor_Tob_C_017: So you had to get this good at it to survive?\nNo wonder your bait worked so well.
MID_SE_Lor_Tob_C_018: I thought you were just a mighty commander. Didn't\nrealize you were a fisherman too.
MID_SE_Lor_Tob_C_019: So, Gramps, you mind letting me in on the secret\nof that bait?
MID_SE_Lor_Tob_C_020: Yeah, sure. I learned it from someone else myself.
MID_SE_Lor_Tob_C_021: {SetColor=Gray}Wait, is this what having a kid is like?{SetColor=Default}
MID_SE_Lor_Tob_C_022: Still waiting on that bait lesson here.
MID_SE_Lor_Tob_C_023: Oh, right! I mash up potatoes, jin ba jiao, and\ndried bugs.
MID_SE_Lor_Tob_C_024: Though shrimp pickled in honey is a better bet for\nlong-term storage. Plus it stays put on the hook.
MID_SE_Lor_Tob_C_025: Ooh. I have honey I can get started with right away.\nThanks for the tip!
MID_SE_Lor_Tob_C_026: But you gotta stop drinking while you fish. I don't\ncare how good you are—that's dangerous.
MID_SE_Lor_Tob_C_027: Hey, on a ship, we'd rather drink wine and mead\nthan water. They keep better.
MID_SE_Lor_Tob_C_028: Baw haw haw! Best of luck, kiddo!
MID_SE_Lor_Tob_B: <EDH>
MID_SE_Lor_Tob_B_001: Back at it, huh? How's that bait working out for you?
MID_SE_Lor_Tob_B_002: It rul— I mean, it's very good.
MID_SE_Lor_Tob_B_003: Huh? Something's fishy here, and it ain't the fish.\nStill not getting any bites?
MID_SE_Lor_Tob_B_004: Eh, it's pretty much— I mean, it is as I expected.\nWay better than— Er, thank you for your help.
MID_SE_Lor_Tob_B_005: Then what's the problem? You're acting kinda funny.
MID_SE_Lor_Tob_B_006: I realized it's not a good idea to get too buddy-buddy\nwith a commander.
MID_SE_Lor_Tob_B_007: Someone from Saramis yelled at me for it, so I'm\ntrying to change my— I mean, mend my behavior.
MID_SE_Lor_Tob_B_008: I guess. But you don't gotta take it that far...
MID_SE_Lor_Tob_B_009: I don't want another lecture from that guy, so I might\nas well stick it out. Uh...Sir.
MID_SE_Lor_Tob_B_010: If it makes you feel better, I did like you said and\nleft the wine at home today.
MID_SE_Lor_Tob_B_011: You didn't have to do that for me. You're a mighty\ncommander, after all.
MID_SE_Lor_Tob_B_012: Alright, I've had it! If you're gonna keep this up,\nI'm gonna go say something to that guy.
MID_SE_Lor_Tob_B_013: Kiddos like you are supposed to be a little rude.\nWhat's the harm in it?
MID_SE_Lor_Tob_B_014: Hey, it was just a warning. No need to get so\nworked up— I mean, upset.
MID_SE_Lor_Tob_B_015: Too late! I don't like that guy getting in the way of\nhaving a good time with you. He killed the mood.
MID_SE_Lor_Tob_B_016: Really? You wanted to hang out with me that much?
MID_SE_Lor_Tob_B_017: Hell yeah. I love playing with kiddos who've got\nsome spirit in 'em.
MID_SE_Lor_Tob_B_018: This mug of mine means I don't often get the chance.\nIt means a lot when someone warms up to me.
MID_SE_Lor_Tob_B_019: Huh... I usually hate it when anyone treats me\nlike a kid.
MID_SE_Lor_Tob_B_020: But coming from this guy, it doesn't piss me off at all.
MID_SE_Lor_Tob_B_021: Look, Tobias, if you say it's fine, then I might as well\ndrop the polite act.
MID_SE_Lor_Tob_B_022: So let's go! Any plans for what we should do today\nafter fishing?
MID_SE_Lor_Tob_B_023: We could play in the water. Oh, or you could hang on\nmy arm and I could spin you around!
MID_SE_Lor_Tob_B_024: The world's our oyster! Baw haw haw!
MID_SE_Lor_Tob_B_025: Hehehe. Which one of us is the kiddo here?